# {app name} — frontend pitfalls ledger

> **This file grows.** Every time a correction has to be made twice — by the
> user to the agent, or in review to the same kind of code — it becomes one
> dated line here. That is the whole mechanism: the agent fails, someone catches
> it, a rule is added, and every later task starts from the improved process.
>
> **Rules for writing an entry.** One line, dated `YYYY-MM-DD`, phrased as the
> rule and not as the story. Say what to do, and (only when it is not obvious)
> what the symptom was, so the next reader can recognise the bug. Delete an entry
> when the code makes it impossible — a lint rule, a type, a deleted feature —
> and say in the commit why.
>
> **What does not belong here:** universal React traps (they live in
> `pitfalls.md`), domain rules (they live in the project's docs), and anything
> nobody has actually got wrong yet. This is a record of bugs paid for, not a
> wish list.
>
> Read it before finishing any frontend change, together with `pitfalls.md`.

